 "result": "All tests pass.\n\n**Root cause:** `Sentinel` members' values are `object()` instances. `enum.Enum.__reduce_ex__` reconstructs members by looking up `self._value_` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d but pickling that raw `object()` value creates a new, non-identical instance, so unpickling raised `ValueError: ... is not a valid Sentinel`. `copy`/`deepcopy` already worked since `Enum` defines `__copy__`/`__deepcopy__` to just return `self`.\n\n**Fix** (`src/click/_utils.py`): overrode `Sentinel.__reduce_ex__` to reconstruct by name (`getattr, (self.__class__, self.name)`) instead of by value, since names are stable and picklable.\n\nAlso added parametrized tests in `tests/test_utils/test_sentinel.py` covering `copy`/`deepcopy`/`pickle` (all protocols) for every `Sentinel` member, and a changelog entry. Full test suite (1928 passed) confirms no regressions.",
